ic creatures with human-like  intelligence and there are also other  people on the surface fighting against  these beast men when they defeat one of  these mecca's kameena decides to hijack  it and pilot it for himself  something that never even occurred to  the humans on the surface but kameena is  the visionary the philosopher he breaks  through the paradigm he keeps moving  forward seeing what the others cannot  see and this is what inspires the other  humans on the surface to follow his  example to hijack other gunmen and to  form a human resistance force against  the beast men in order to emphasize  again the importance of all of this and  of Plato's allegory of the cave in  episode 5 Simone kameena and the others  who now follow them on their quest to  defeat the beast men stumble into  another underground village by accident  in this village called a die the gunmen  mecha are worshipped like gods  and when kameena tells them that the  gunmen are not gods but merely mecca's  piloted by beast men they get upset  because he is challenging their  long-held beliefs again coming up lays  the role of the philosopher he searches  for the truth and for justice and he  cannot understand that there are people  out there who are willing to live a lie  just because it's easier than accepting  the truth  commie name and says that he would  rather die than live this way he always  looks outside the box outside the cave  he is a leader and a visionary and his  behavior can appear completely  irrational to others because he rushes  into headfirst into battles and believes  that his manly spirit and willpower is  all he needs to destroy any enemy  kameena is an idealist someone who  always looks forward and yearns for  truth and justice someone who is never  satisfied with the status quo some have  said that communist just crazy and  reckless or dumb to use screwattack's  terminology fricking ScrewAttack but to  be fair the list of people who think  this about kameena includes  not only some viewers of the anime but  also many of the characters in the  actual show however rather than being  crazy or dumb kameena is exactly the  type of person humanity needs in that  moment in time in the horribly bleak and  dangerous situation that humans find  themselves in within the caves and on  the surface common sense is not enough  being reasonable and practical is not  enough if we think about the situation  in terms of common sense it's clear that  the beastmen are way more powerful at  the beginning of the series and a  practical person in that moment in time  will conclude that the beastmen will  inevitably win and that resistance is  therefore futile I mean the beastmen  have superior numbers superior weaponry  superior Intel superior everything but  kameena takes it upon himself to be the  symbol and the pillar of hope for others  he refuses to accept the so-called  inevitable he thinks outside the box and  by seeing his example and following it  the other humans on the surface become  hopeful and confident that they can  actually make a difference and fight  back against the enemy kameena is a true  visionary leader exactly the type of  leader humanity needs at that point  which is why the others follow him even  though he might seem crazy to some we  have to remember that geniuses often do  for example Nikola Tesla was called  crazy when in the late 1800s he  advocated for alternating currents as  superior to the more established direct  current that was being pushed by Thomas  Edison in the end alternating current  one and we all use it to power our homes  today Steve Jobs was also called crazy  for thinking that everyone will one day  own a personal computer in their homes  way back when computers were the size of  an entire room and I think we all know  how that turned out and just like these  visionaries from our own world  kameena was called crazy from wanting to  leave the cave and from wanting to fight  against seemingly impossible 